WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — ai-coding-market (45s) Narrator Osato

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.411
First, headline trillion-dollar figures for AI coding are future guesses, not counts of money already earned.

2
00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:14.678
Second, almost every forecast assumes developers will pay a giant AI model by the word forever.

3
00:00:15.118 --> 00:00:20.971
Third, saving and reusing working code drives repeated jobs toward electricity cost,

4
00:00:20.971 --> 00:00:23.200
making those forecasts too high.

5
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.467
Open compilers, web servers, and code libraries create trillions of dollars in

6
00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:33.975
business value without charging developers a toll every time a program compiles. Treating

7
00:00:33.975 --> 00:00:38.863
every routine code edit as a fresh cloud conversation confuses value with rent.

8
00:00:39.303 --> 00:00:43.638
When an AI solves a class of problem once and engineers lock that

9
00:00:43.638 --> 00:00:49.307
verified fix into a fast local tool, repeated work drops toward raw electricity cost.
